## Desk outcome

The desk's engineering update reports #4471 **closed on 5 October**, with one outcome per problem:

| problem | public ticket | desk outcome |
| --- | --- | --- |
| shared month-first parser (379 reports) | [#2](https://github.com/keaglin/mega-dev-support-kb/issues/2) | **fixed**: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| booking-v3 month-first hint (33 reports) | [#1](https://github.com/keaglin/mega-dev-support-kb/issues/1) | **won't fix**: booking-v3 form retired |

These outcomes come from the desk's update, not from this KB. The export contains no product code,
so this review records them as reported and does not reproduce the fix. The two outcomes differ,
which confirms #4471 held two problems, not one.

## Keep routing separate from causal hypotheses

Placement in this table describes the exported ticket, not current public issue state or confirmed causation.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

### Parser hypothesis in the supplied model

The model describes a shared month-first parser receiving a day-first tenant's input. Report
`R-41203` describes 2 December becoming 12 February, which is compatible with that explanation.
The report does not supply the original numeric entry or a processing trace that proves it.

### Hint hypothesis in the supplied model

The model describes booking-v3 displaying `MM/DD/YYYY` while its form reads the tenant's
day-first convention. Report `R-41241` describes 6 August becoming 8 June, which is compatible
with that path if the directory's form facts applied when the report arrived.
The report does not capture the actual hint or entry, and the directory has no form-version history.

These mechanisms can produce the same visible swap. `R-41416` and `R-41482`, from the same tenant,
contain identical wording but receive different buckets because their channels differ. The
reported date pair alone cannot decide between the model's explanations.

## Read the report descriptions independently

The body audit recognizes exactly two English day/month descriptions with exchanged numeric
components. It infers no year, raw input format or production cause. A body without that complete
pair is not thereby a false positive or a new defect. The figures below are computed from the
unchanged report records, separately from the routing rule.

<Review4471 />

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The **exported page's original 30 September review date** precedes the latest reports in that
export. The current incident page's review date records our later KB correction, not an earlier
product diagnosis. Neither a merge timestamp nor a queued fix proves shipment or recovery.

The desk's original flags and the body-audit gaps are different evidence sets. A month/day swap
does not establish why a report describes a one-day discrepancy or an invite preceding a booking;
different local weekdays can also be legitimate views of one instant. These reports need an
explicit disposition, not a blanket causal claim.

## Policy status and classifier limits

[Accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) records the subject-only policy
approved in June 2024. The [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) now marks its recorded merge instructions
as under review and links this investigation. This factual correction does not approve a replacement
policy. The comparison below uses tenant, locale, form and channel to illustrate classifier buckets,
not to establish production causation or authorize a merge.

This compares the exported date classifier, not production reproductions or an approved merge policy.
Matching bucket labels require corroboration of the reported failure mechanism.

<DedupeExplorer />

The concrete counterexamples matter: Alder form versus app has the same subject but different buckets;
Copper versus Morrow form traffic has the same subject/channel but different buckets; Pale versus Alder
form traffic can have different subjects yet the same hint bucket. An unknown tenant is unclassified.
Even equal non-null buckets need corroborated failure evidence before they establish shared causation.

[Proposed decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-evidence-based-triage) separates report identity,
provisional routing, causal merges and unresolved evidence. It is not adopted and does not
silently replace accepted decision 0001. Matching a documented failure mechanism is its proposed
basis for causal merges; equal subjects or equal buckets alone are not enough.

## Desk action and verification limits

- Preserve the existing routing membership while distinguishing the original desk flags from all body-evidence gaps.
- Public tracking is [parser issue #2](https://github.com/keaglin/mega-dev-support-kb/issues/2)
  and [hint issue #1](https://github.com/keaglin/mega-dev-support-kb/issues/1). Per the desk's update,
  #2 closes as fixed and #1 closes as won't fix because the booking-v3 form is retired.
- The nine body-evidence gaps stay inside the parser count; the desk's fix does not establish
  that each of them was a month/day swap.
- The supplied 4 October export remains the bounded evidence set; the desk's update is the only later input used.

